   | Raw readout is best at B=32 (77.66%): the shared-Rsense loading gain grows with column
   | height, so the larger blocks that win on energy lose catastrophically on accuracy.
   | After per-column gain calibration the best is B=128 (92.81%), and the cost varies
   | by 0.00 pts across B.
   | 
   | If the calibrated cost is ~0 at every B, then this model's entire 'analog error'
   | was a deterministic scale factor and the SNR_analog column in every earlier CSV
   | overstates the penalty. That is the expected outcome -- the model is noiseless, so
   | every error in it is systematic. It does NOT mean a real crossbar is free: device
   | variability, read noise, drift and ADC quantisation are all absent here, and they
   | are what actually sets the analog floor. Say so explicitly in the paper.
